#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## Embed on a corpus small enough to read: twelve sentences about pets
## and food. Run with "just demo-lib Embed pets".

"em:" u_se< "Embed"

## Words: 1 the, 2 cat, 3 dog, 4 eats, 5 fish, 6 meat, 7 sleeps, 8 runs.
## Each pet with each food and each action, so the two keep the same
## company. Sentences as word numbers, each ended by 0.
ids := 1 2 4 5 0 1 2 4 6 0 1 3 4 5 0 1 3 4 6 0 1 2 7 0 1 2 8 0 1 3 7 0 1 3 8 0 2 4 5 0 3 4 6 0 2 8 0 3 7 0
C := (8, 2) em:c_ooccur ids
## Who keeps whose company: the counts, then weighted.
C
P := em:p_pmi C
(f_loat f_loor 0.5 + 100.0 * P) / 100.0
## cat's 3 nearest (by cosine of the PPMI rows): the, eats, dog. In a
## dozen sentences "the" and "eats" keep company with every pet, so
## they look like the cat as much as the dog does. Repeating the same
## sentences would change nothing (PPMI is a ratio); more varied ones
## would: on the embedding explorer's corpus a word's nearest is of
## its own kind for 33% of words at 12 sentences, 91% at 200 and 90%
## from 1,600 on (its README has the table).
(P, 3) em:n_earest 2
## fish's 3 nearest: meat, the other food, first.
(P, 3) em:n_earest 5
